I've installed UCX 2.0 (aka DEC TCP/IP) on my system and cannot get outward
mail configured properly.  Telnet/FTP/incomming SMTP works fine.  The
name (bind) resolver is working correctly.

Whenever I try to post mail off system I basically end up with a
situation in which the STMP server symbiont queue dies a horrible death.

I get OPCOM messages complaining of problems with mailboxes, ultimately
leading to an access violation in the symbiont while in module
smtp$do_task.  The log files are not otherwise very helpful.  

I don't have any records loaded for routing (MX_records), so I'm wondering
if this is where things are amiss.   I have RTFMs, but I can't say that
I've really integrated all the material in a useful fashion in my brain yet.

CSC/DSIN has not be able to help or reproduce the problem,  so I was
wondering if anyone has seen/cured anything similiar.





